.TH LAUNCHER-EDITOR 1 "October 2026" "Launcher Editor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
launcher-editor \- manage Freedesktop desktop entries and application icons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launcher-editor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Launcher Editor
is a graphical utility for managing the application entries that appear in
Linux desktop launchers and on the desktop.
.PP
It reads desktop entries from the XDG data directories, including Flatpak and
Snap export directories, and distinguishes user entries from system entries.
System entries are read-only.  Hiding a system entry writes a small override
file in the user application directory; the package-managed file is never
modified.
.PP
The application can create and edit user desktop entries, validate them with
.BR desktop-file-validate (1),
place executable shortcuts on the desktop, and import images into the user
hicolor icon theme at several sizes.
.PP
All write operations are limited to the user's home directory.  The program
does not require root privileges and does not access the network.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications
User desktop entries and system-entry suppression overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor
Custom icons imported by the application.
.TP
.I ~/.config/launcher-editor/config.json
Window and filter preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/launcher-editor/icons.json
Manifest of icons imported by the application.
.TP
.I $XDG_DESKTOP_DIR
Desktop shortcuts created by the application.  The location is resolved with
.BR xdg-user-dir (1)
or the XDG user directories configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR desktop-file-validate (1),
.BR update-desktop-database (1),
.BR xdg-user-dir (1)
.PP
The Desktop Entry Specification:
.IR https://specifications.freedesktop.org/desktop-entry-spec/ .
.SH AUTHOR
Launcher Editor contributors.
